files.change:
Add the occurrence stamp. Filename takes the current epoch-milliseconds timestamp per packages/loot-core/migrations/README.md. Exact body:

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
ALTER TABLE transactions ADD COLUMN schedule_occurrence INTEGER DEFAULT NULL;
COMMIT;

The column MUST be INTEGER, not TEXT: date columns are stored as INTEGER yyyymmdd by toDateRepr, and declaring the stamp TEXT makes AQL's date conversion throw 'fromDateRepr not passed a number'. It must be nullable with default NULL, which packages/loot-core/migrations/README.md lists under 'Allowed changes' after the cutoff ('Add a nullable column, or a NOT NULL column with a DEFAULT') and which is what makes the legacy fallback possible. transactions is a synced table and keeps its single id primary key; nothing is dropped or renamed. I ran the repo's own guard against this file unmodified: src/server/migrate/additive-migrations.test.ts passes 40/40.
